.Dd November 1, 2026
.Dt CMUS 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm cmus
.Nd play music in the terminal
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl \-listen Ar socket
.Op Fl \-show\-cursor
.Nm
.Fl \-plugins | \-help | \-version
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a music player for the terminal, with a library, playlists and a play
queue, which
.Xr cmus-remote 1
controls from another shell.
It is installed in the GNU root.
.Pp
It plays through OSS: it writes
.Pa /dev/dsp
and sets the PCM channel of
.Pa /dev/mixer ,
which scales only the sound cmus itself plays, mixed with that of every
other program.
.Xr mixer 1
reads its own PCM level and cannot show cmus's.
It reads WAV itself, and MP3, FLAC, Ogg Vorbis, Opus, AAC and the other
types its FFmpeg input lists through FFmpeg's libraries; CUE sheets name
tracks in another file.
.Pp
Press 1 to 7 to change the view: the library as a tree and as a list, the
playlists, the play queue, the file browser, the filters and the settings.
In the browser,
.Ic a
adds the file or directory under the cursor to the library and
.Ic enter
plays it.
.Ic c
pauses,
.Ic v
stops,
.Ic b
plays the next track,
.Ic z
the one before,
.Ic \-
and
.Ic +
change the volume by 10%, the left and right arrows seek, and
.Ic q
quits.
A colon begins a command, such as
.Ql :add ~/music
or
.Ql :set softvol=true .
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl \-listen Ar socket
Listen for
.Xr cmus-remote 1
on
.Ar socket
instead of the default.
.It Fl \-show\-cursor
Always show the cursor.
.It Fl \-plugins
List the input and output plugins and the file types of each, and exit.
.It Fl \-help
Print the usage and exit.
.It Fl \-version
Print the version and exit.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
.It Ev CMUS_HOME
The configuration directory, by default
.Pa ~/.config/cmus .
.It Ev CMUS_SOCKET
The socket
.Xr cmus-remote 1
connects to, by default
.Pa $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/cmus-socket ,
or
.Pa socket
in the configuration directory where
.Ev XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
is not set.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /usr/share/cmus/rc
.It Pa /dev/dsp
The OSS device it plays on.
.It Pa /dev/mixer
The mixer whose PCM channel its volume sets.
.It Pa ~/.config/cmus/autosave
The settings and key bindings, written on exit.
.It Pa ~/.config/cmus/rc
Commands read at start, after the saved settings.
.It Pa /usr/share/cmus/rc
The default settings, read when there is no autosave file.
.It Pa /usr/lib/cmus
The input plugins, in
.Pa ip ,
and the output plugin, in
.Pa op .
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Play the files under
.Pa ~/music :
start
.Nm ,
type
.Ql :add ~/music ,
press 2 and then enter on a track.
.Pp
Use the program's own volume instead of the mixer's PCM channel:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
:set softvol=true
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cmus-remote 1 ,
.Xr ffmpeg 1 ,
.Xr mixer 1 ,
.Xr dsp 4 ,
.Xr mixer 4 ,
.Xr cmus-tutorial 7
.Pp
.Nm man
shows the upstream manual of
.Nm ,
which lists every command and setting, on the GNU system, where
.Nm
is a port's.
.Sh LIMITS
OSS is the only output.
There is no CD input and no MPRIS.
Tags are read through FFmpeg, which does not read every tag the upstream's
own decoder plugins do.
